(6073931, 892907, 39343, '<td valign="top">Wow - I certainly wasn''t expecting a ribbon, much less a blue one!  Thank you very much to everyone who voted and especially everyone who commented!  So a little about the image - I''ve been playing around with op art style images off and on for a while now and when challenge subject of books came up, this concept popped into my head almost immediately.  A quick search and then a wait for the library system to ship the book to my local branch and I was ready to shoot.  For those wondering, the book is Introducing Op Art by John Lancaster.  As for the suit - it''s called a zentai suit and can be found in a number of places in the wonderful world that is the Internet.  I''ve found them particularly inspiring and visually cool for photographic work (not to mention they''re comfy! :) ).  A good solid branch of my work is based in this - have a look for me on Flickr if you want to check out more...<br/> <br/>Thanks again, everyone!</td>', 'Wow - I certainly wasn''t expecting a ribbon, much less a blue one!  Thank you very much to everyone who voted and especially everyone who commented!  So a little about the image - I''ve been playing around with op art style images off and on for a while now and when challenge subject of books came up, this concept popped into my head almost immediately.  A quick search and then a wait for the library system to ship the book to my local branch and I was ready to shoot.  For those wondering, the book is Introducing Op Art by John Lancaster.  As for the suit - it''s called a zentai suit and can be found in a number of places in the wonderful world that is the Internet.  I''ve found them particularly inspiring and visually cool for photographic work (not to mention they''re comfy! :) ).  A good solid branch of my work is based in this - have a look for me on Flickr if you want to check out more... Thanks again, everyone!', '2010-06-30 03:33:14.000000', NULL, 0),
