(6074446, 893040, 68947, '<td valign="top">Thank you Michelle and Steve! :)  <br/> <br/>I don''t know if it''s my eyes (cataracts) or what gives but, I cannot see the "oof" in this shot on the books???  I have a new monitor too! LOL  Perhaps, it''s that my eyes aren''t trained to see these things well?????  Maybe, it was that my camera was too close...or, maybe, it was my processing????  I think Steve is right in saying that the background was too strong.  I have to learn to select properly and then, I can manipulate the backgrounds a bit better.  Gotta learn how to mask properly rather than the selection tools which are time consuming and less accurate.  Thanks to you both for commenting! :)</td>', 'Thank you Michelle and Steve! :)   I don''t know if it''s my eyes (cataracts) or what gives but, I cannot see the "oof" in this shot on the books???  I have a new monitor too! LOL  Perhaps, it''s that my eyes aren''t trained to see these things well?????  Maybe, it was that my camera was too close...or, maybe, it was my processing????  I think Steve is right in saying that the background was too strong.  I have to learn to select properly and then, I can manipulate the backgrounds a bit better.  Gotta learn how to mask properly rather than the selection tools which are time consuming and less accurate.  Thanks to you both for commenting! :)', '2010-06-30 13:24:04.000000', NULL, 0),
