(6085496, 893015, 95118, '<td valign="top">For all those who asked about why she was reading a music book- she''s a concert pianist and she was studying her favorite score. Thanks for the votes.</td>', 'For all those who asked about why she was reading a music book- she''s a concert pianist and she was studying her favorite score. Thanks for the votes.', '2010-07-08 13:14:22.000000', NULL, 0),
(6093188, 892948, 61084, '<td valign="top">Hi Serena. I like what you were trying to do here, and things get better over time. A bit of advice is what your shutter speed. 1/2 sec is too slow to hand hold the camera and get clarity. It will be too soft or blurry from even the slightest movement. Even if you have to purchase a cheap tripod to start out with it will help you a lot in times like this.<br/> <br/>The photo size has already been mentioned, and you will learn the best way to size your images in time. I would also shoot this at a much lower view point instead of being so far above and shooting downward. Try being say a foot or two above the level of the book and angling down a little, but not as drastic as you did here.<br/> <br/>So with those three considerations of using a tripod, uploading a bigger image and changing your shooting angle a little and maybe more light...especially on the right side of the photo I think this would have scored a bit higher.<br/> <br/>You will pick up all kinds of pointers and ideas here, and learn as you look at what others have done to be successful. Only challenge number 1 so don''t fret and shrug it off.<br/> <br/>Good luck in your future challenges!<br/> <br/>David<br/></td>', 'Hi Serena. I like what you were trying to do here, and things get better over time. A bit of advice is what your shutter speed. 1/2 sec is too slow to hand hold the camera and get clarity. It will be too soft or blurry from even the slightest movement. Even if you have to purchase a cheap tripod to start out with it will help you a lot in times like this. The photo size has already been mentioned, and you will learn the best way to size your images in time. I would also shoot this at a much lower view point instead of being so far above and shooting downward. Try being say a foot or two above the level of the book and angling down a little, but not as drastic as you did here. So with those three considerations of using a tripod, uploading a bigger image and changing your shooting angle a little and maybe more light...especially on the right side of the photo I think this would have scored a bit higher. You will pick up all kinds of pointers and ideas here, and learn as you look at what others have done to be successful. Only challenge number 1 so don''t fret and shrug it off. Good luck in your future challenges! David', '2010-07-14 20:33:00.000000', NULL, 0),
(6105578, 893119, 40391, '<td valign="top">I thought this was a lovely photo that I gave an 8 and I''m not surprised it finished so high (though I thought it was a top 10 - so close). I''d say keep reading but the ceiling is not that high.<br/> <br/>Lovely lighting and the composition is great - well done!</td>', 'I thought this was a lovely photo that I gave an 8 and I''m not surprised it finished so high (though I thought it was a top 10 - so close). I''d say keep reading but the ceiling is not that high. Lovely lighting and the composition is great - well done!', '2010-07-27 06:21:25.000000', NULL, 0),
